-- title:
--   Compositum coordinates for a Galois and a cyclic layer
-- statement:
--   Let $E, F, L, N$ be number fields with $F$, $L$ and $N$ algebras over $E$ and $N$ an algebra over both $F$ and $L$, the two towers $E \subseteq F \subseteq N$ and $E \subseteq L \subseteq N$ being compatible as scalar towers, and with $F/E$, $L/E$ and $N/E$ Galois. Assume that $\mathrm{Gal}(L/E) = L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]} L$ is cyclic, that $[L:E] = [F:E]$ as $E$-dimensions, and that every $E$-automorphism $\sigma$ of $N$ which fixes $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,F\,N(x)$ for all $x \in F$ and $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,L\,N(y)$ for all $y \in L$ is the identity. Write $\Gamma = N \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]} N$, and let $S$ and $T$ be the fixing subgroups in $\Gamma$ of the field ranges of the structure maps $F \to N$ and $L \to N$ respectively. The conclusion asserts, as nested existentials over proofs that $S$ and $T$ are normal in $\Gamma$, that: $S \sqcap T = \bot$; $\mathrm{Nat.card}(\Gamma/S) = \mathrm{Nat.card}(F \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]} F)$; there is an element $s$ of $\Gamma/T$ whose integer powers exhaust $\Gamma/T$ and whose order equals $\mathrm{Nat.card}(\Gamma/S)$; and there is an element $t$ of $S$ whose integer powers exhaust $S$.
--
--   This is the group-theoretic bookkeeping of the classical compositum construction: over the base $E$ one records a Galois layer $F$ and a cyclic layer $L$ of the same degree inside a common Galois $N$ generated by the two, obtaining $\Gamma/S \cong \mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$, $\Gamma/T$ cyclic of that same order, $S \cap T = 1$ and $S$ cyclic. It is used in the Herbrand-quotient computation [`M4aHerbrand.exists_natCard_H2_eq_card_and_span_eq_top_ideleClassGroup`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.exists_natCard_H2_eq_card_and_span_eq_top_ideleClassGroup).
